# Copy to /etc/igor/env (systemd) or .env (compose). Contains credentials: chmod 600.
#
# Seat tokens belong here, because a seat is a subscription several Igors may draw from. The
# GitHub App does not: each role acts as its own, from a per-instance file,
# /etc/igor/<role>.env, at the end of this one.
#
# Under systemd, a seat token may instead be a `LoadCredential=` a seat's `token_file` names —
# see the commented-out example in igor.service and docs/deployment.md. That keeps the token
# out of this unit's environment entirely; nothing below does.

# One per seat, named by `token_env` in igor.config.yaml. The convention is IGOR_SEAT_ plus
# the seat's id, uppercased, with anything but a letter or digit becoming an underscore — so
# a seat `fleet-1` reads IGOR_SEAT_FLEET_1 and a seat `adam` reads IGOR_SEAT_ADAM.
#
# From `claude setup-token` run while signed in as that seat. A seat naming a variable that is
# unset is skipped, never substituted with whatever login is ambient.
IGOR_SEAT_FLEET_1=
IGOR_SEAT_ADAM=

# --- /etc/igor/<role>.env, one per Igor ---

# The GitHub App this Igor acts as: every gh and git call it makes carries a token minted from
# these, and nothing else. GITHUB_APP_IDENTITY must be the role's name. Give exactly one of
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE or GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY; with both, the Igor refuses to start.
# This file and the key are 0600 and owned by the service user. No GH_TOKEN: Igor ignores
# one. Creating the App: docs/deployment.md, "Giving an Igor its GitHub App".
GITHUB_APP_IDENTITY=maintenance
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/etc/igor/maintenance.pem

# Only for the github-app skill's `check`, where the App is installed on more than one account.
# Igor ignores both and finds its installation from its repositories.
#GITHUB_APP_OWNER=
#GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
